{
 "section_summary": "This section contains translated Japanese commercial messages intercepted at Chungking in November and December 1943, with two U.S. Embassy despatches forwarding the translations. The messages concern trade quotas, shipping, permits, barter, prices, rice, textiles, rubber, medicines, and wartime business reorganization across East and Southeast Asia. It ends with a London Embassy despatch forwarding a Financial Times article on Japan’s economic difficulties and the first page of that article.",
